topics.detail:
AI Not Welcome argues that AI undermines human creativity. AI does not provide essential needs like food and shelter. AI Impact argues that AI will monitor networks and infrastructure. AI code is becoming more reliable.

@zachweinersmith.bsky.social: “Reddit stock got crushed today. Interesting thing is on the earnings call they specifically cited AI as disrupting traffic. I enjoy (well-curated reddit), but it's a bit rich hearing social media networks complaining about a third party getting paid for their content!”

AI Not Welcome (78.9%) says AI is not helpful. AI Impact (21.1%) says AI is affecting various aspects of online life.

AI Harms Society argues that AI has negative impacts. AI Transparency argues that AI-generated content must be identifiable. AI-generated political ads need prominent labeling. AI-generated artwork accusations harm artists.

@boneydiego.bsky.social: “The scourge that this whole "industry" is. Generative AI has zero good uses and you cannot convince me otherwise. Burn it all down.”

AI Harms Society (78.1%) says AI has negative impacts. AI Transparency (21.9%) says AI content should be identified.

AI Harms World argues that AI usage is harmful. AI makes work more frustrating. AI displaces human time and effort. AI is pervasive and devalues human time. AI Falls Short argues that AI can be right but still lose. AI has a limited life cycle. AI can be filtered out by smart people.

@ealgumby.bsky.social: “The point of the episode is PARTICULARLY PERTINENT TODAY, as we struggle with the role of AI... Here's the thing: AI can be 'right' (commit no mistakes), and STILL LOSE! If one is adept (as I might be) at predicting AI response, it becomes a joke to make it 'lose' all the time.”

AI Harms World (53.3%) says AI is harmful to the world. AI Falls Short (46.7%) says AI is flawed.

World.detail:
Israel Politics argues that Israel's government excludes Arab citizens. Democrats who support Israel are Zionists. Israel's democracy requires Jewish-Arab partnership. Israel meddles in European elections. Israel's government cannot be formed without Arab parties. US Aid argues that US aid to Israel benefits the Military Industrial Complex. Israel's government is genocidal and hypocritical. US aid to Israel fuels land-grabbing wars. Israel is not a US ally and does not deserve aid.

@tadhgdalaigh.bsky.social: “Israel is NOT an ally.”

Israel Politics (76.7%) says Israel's government formation is problematic. US Aid (23.3%) says US aid to Israel is unnecessary.

Gaza Crisis argues that Gaza is beyond acceptable. Gaza is a genocide. Gaza is an orchestrated campaign. Gaza is like a prison. Gaza needs Palestinian-led recovery. Palestine Support argues that Symbolic support for fighting oppression. Lacking direct support for the Palestinian cause.

@thetnholler.bsky.social: “CHANNEL FOUR: “Gaza is a mass grave with rubble instead of headstones””

Gaza Crisis (93.5%) says Gaza situation is unacceptable. Palestine Support (6.5%) says Palestine support is symbolic.

Politics.detail:
Trans Rights argues that watching Harry Potter shows indifference to trans people. Transphobes prioritize hate over women's and trans issues. Cis people often make thoughtless comments to trans individuals. Transphobia is a real threat to trans lives. Trans people are excluded from discussions about trans issues. Trans women face unique challenges and stereotypes. Trans Rights argues that abandoning trans people won't gain votes. trans people won't vote for transphobic Democrats. only trans people and right-wing bigots care about trans issues. some Democrats are transphobic. Democrats may adopt anti-trans sentiments. attacking trans people is not safe politically.

@ravenlynclemens.bsky.social: “it's fine to point out stuff like a lot of trans women are in stem or whatever. it's weird when people act like elitist snobs about conforming to the correct transgender aesthetics. maybe this is all just in my head idk”

Trans Rights (51.3%) says Trans people face prejudice. Trans Rights (48.7%) says Democrats should support trans people.

Business.detail:
Billionaire Greed argues that Billionaires are out of control and prioritize their wealth over others. Billionaires' greed is destroying the planet and its resources. Corporate Risk argues that Circular deals pose a risk to companies.

@debbie156.bsky.social: “Chevron has tripled their profits. 9.9 billion. Trump is bragging that “we are making a fortune…” When he says “We” he most definitely does not mean you or me. Yes-Trump did this with his illegal war. Yes-Big Oil is taking advantage & gouging us.”

Billionaire Greed (90.6%) says Billionaires are too greedy. Corporate Risk (9.4%) says Circular deals pose a risk to companies.

Environment.detail:
Data Centers argues that Data centers waste water and energy. Data centers are unnecessary and corrupt. Data centers harm local ecosystems. Data centers promote centralized control. Data Privacy argues that Companies will sell customer data to the government. Data is being stolen from the people. Data brokers should be targeted to protect information. Data collection prioritized over climate change. Individuals are unable to control their own data.

@marypeltola.com: “Dan Sullivan owns up to $5 million in his family’s company. His brother, the CEO, says it’s on track for more than $100 million a year in data-center sales. Is it any wonder Dan’s pitching data centers to Big Tech and inviting them to build in Alaska?”

Data Centers (82.5%) says Data centers are problematic. Data Privacy (17.5%) says Government and companies misuse personal data.
